{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966823,"nonce":"ria2po4rUH14QQgtdGSQYvHiMsU=","title":"Multi-module .blinc compilation plan","message":"Goal: real apps need multiple `.blinc` files (one per component or grouping), cross-file references, and per-file hot reload. Today `BlincDsl::compile_source` ingests one source string at a time; substrate registries are process-global (FSM, component, signal, value-returning-views set).\n\n**Why:** Without this, user apps are stuck inlining everything into one giant file. Component reuse across screens and per-file hot reload (the common dev-loop case) both block on it.\n\n**How to apply:** Build the phases in order; each phase is independently shippable and unblocks real usage.\n\n- `BlincDsl::compile_directory(path)` — walk `.blinc` files in a dir, compile each via existing `compile_source`.\n- Per-file `compiled_modules` map tracks emitted JIT function names so `recompile_file` can replay just that subset.\n- Beadie's atomic `swap_compiled` handles function-pointer swap; substrate state (FSM / signal / component registries) persists across reloads.\n- **Limits:** no module decls, no FQN call sites yet. Two files with `component Counter` collide.\n\n**Syntax follows ES6/TypeScript**, NOT Rust. No `::` paths, no `mod` blocks. Commit 2436a2ba already pinned dot-notation via field access.\n\nDSL surface:\n```\n// Named imports — most common path.\nimport { Counter, Button } from \"./ui/widgets\"\nview { Counter() }\n\n// Namespace import — alternative.\nimport * as widgets from \"./ui/widgets\"\nview { widgets.Counter() }\n```\n\nField access (`widgets.Counter`) already parses through the existing `suffix_field` postfix layer — no new path-syntax grammar needed. Capital-leading final segment disambiguates a component reference from a method call (existing Blinc convention).\n\nWhat Zyntax provides (don't reinvent):\n- `TypedDeclaration::Import(TypedImport { module_path, items })` + `TypedImportItem::Named { name, alias } | Glob | Default` — ES6 import shapes in the typed AST.\n- `TypedDeclaration::Module(TypedModule)` for declared modules (file-derived modules don't need an explicit decl).\n- `ImportResolver` trait (`zyntax_typed_ast::import_resolver`) with `resolve_import` / `module_exists` / `get_module_exports` / `resolve_qualified_type` + `ChainedResolver`.\n- `ZyntaxRuntime::add_filesystem_resolver(base, \"blinc\")` — convention-based file lookup; module path `foo.bar` → `base/foo/bar.blinc` or `base/foo.bar.blinc`.\n- `ZyntaxRuntime::add_import_resolver(callback)` — closure-based resolver for custom routing.\n- `CompilationConfig.import_resolver` — the lowering pipeline consumes it.\n\nWhat Blinc adds:\n- Grammar: an `import_stmt` rule at the top of a `.blinc` file matching ES6 `import { X, Y } from \"./path\"` / `import * as ns from \"./path\"` / `import Default from \"./path\"`. Lowers to `TypedDeclaration::Import` with the corresponding `TypedImportItem` shape.\n- `BlincDsl::compile_project(entry, source_root)`: wires `add_filesystem_resolver(source_root, \"blinc\")` and compiles from a single entry source. Zyntax's import resolver pulls dependent files on demand.\n- File→module convention: file path under the source root IS the dotted module path (`ui/widgets.blinc` → `ui.widgets`); matches `add_filesystem_resolver`. No source-level `module foo { ... }` decl needed — file path is the identity, ES6-style.\n- Substrate registry: Zyntax's module-prefixed mangling (whatever scheme it produces for cross-module symbol references) becomes the `view_symbol` on each component def — we register what Zyntax produces, don't rekey our registry.\n- Diagnostics: surfaced through Zyntax's existing `ImportError` types.\n\n**Import shape gaps (upstream Zyntax patches needed):**\n- Per-item alias `import { A as B }` — `TypedImportItem` has the field, but `parsed_value_to_import_items` only emits `Named { alias: None }`. Need to teach the action-language interpreter to recognize `(name, alias)` shapes, OR add a Blinc-side post-parse rename pass.\n- `import *` wildcard — `TypedImportItem::Glob` is constructed for the literal `\"*\"`, but `process_imports_for_traits` flat-merges every non-Import decl regardless of items shape, so wildcards are a no-op vs named imports.\n- `import * as ns from \"./mod\"` namespace alias — Zyntax encodes via top-level `alias` field, but flat-merge gives `ns.X` no runtime namespace to resolve against. Needs either (a) Zyntax-side module scoping with prefixed symbols, or (b) Blinc-side post-parse pass that rewrites namespace-aliased access to flat symbols.\n- `import Default from \"./mod\"` — `TypedImportItem::Default(name)` exists; needs `export default` story (Phase C).\n\nPragmatic stance for now: keep grammar at named-only. Surface a clean diagnostic for `import *` / `import * as` / `import Default` until the upstream gap closes.\n\nOpen questions to verify before implementing:\n- How does Zyntax lower a cross-module symbol reference (after an `import` resolves it) to a JIT symbol name? Defines our `view_symbol` convention for module-scoped components.\n- Does Zyntax's `add_filesystem_resolver` auto-wrap the loaded file in a `TypedModule`, or does the source need an explicit module decl? (For ES6 parity, auto-wrap from file path is what we want.)\n- Glob imports (`import * as widgets`) — does the resolver bring all `export`s into a namespace under the alias, or does it require subsequent field access through a runtime namespace object?\n\n- `export component Counter` / `export fn` / `export signal` to publish; default = private to the file. Matches ES6 named exports.\n- Optional sugar: `export default component Foo { ... }` for the file's primary export, importable as `import Foo from \"./path\"`.\n- Resolver enforces: imports of non-`export`ed names fail with `ImportError::SymbolNotFound`.\n- Builtins (`Div`, `Text`, `#[extern_widget]`-registered Rust widgets) are implicitly exported and globally visible — they live in the substrate registry, not in any module's source.\n\n- `blinc.toml` (or convention) for entry point + watched paths.\n- File watcher → incremental recompile pipeline. Track which files depend on which so a change in `widgets.blinc` rebuilds importers.\n- Source maps: errors point at the originating file:line, not just the module-mangled symbol.\n\n- Generic types / generics across modules — separate slice, depends on Zyntax-side generic support.\n- Cyclic imports — error out for v1.\n- Package registry / crates-style versioning.","files":null}]}